From 3201b5e90e84a0f34381506a71ee64c7f08ccdbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:07:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 187/194] phy: qcom-mipi-csi2: Add the SM8750 v2.3.0 D-PHY
 sequence

Use the non-combo D-PHY sequence from the published SM8750 GPL camera
driver instead of assigning the X1E80100 table to this hardware. Preserve
all 103 table entries and lane ordering, the 209-us preparation delays,
zero writes when deskew is disabled, and the -10 settle-count adjustment.
Hold reset across reference-generator polling and lane programming, then
release it with the v2.3.0 D-PHY value. Restore reset before clocks stop.

Keep PHY interrupts masked because the generic PHY has no interrupt
handler. Reject unsupported polarity/deskew configurations and invalid
lane or settle-count settings. Hardware version reading is optional so
this variant does not issue the X1E revision-register selector sequence.
The CAMCC timer clock has a single supported 400-MHz rate.

Source: lenovo-basements/android_kernel_lenovo_sm8750-modules
Commit: e1f324632d70b2427751820cd48eefc45baab0ce
Files: qcom/opensource/camera-kernel/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/
       include/cam_csiphy_2_3_0_hwreg.h, cam_csiphy_core.c, cam_csiphy_soc.c

Validation: ARM64 GCC14.2 W=1 object build; checkpatch; actual candidate C
code run against mocked MMIO, compared with independently parsed stock
GPL tables for 24 configurations and two start/stop cycles each, plus
14 error/timeout cases and sparse lane mapping. No hardware test or board
DT enablement; sensor and CAMSS980 integration remain incomplete.
